# ☁️ AWS Resource List Checker

> A shell script to list all active AWS resources across multiple services in any region — built for DevOps Engineers who need a quick infrastructure overview.

---

## 📋 Resources Covered

| # | AWS Service | What it lists |
|---|-------------|---------------|
| 1 | EC2 | Instance ID, Type, State, IP, Name |
| 2 | S3 | Bucket names + creation date |
| 3 | VPC | VPC ID, CIDR, State, Name |
| 4 | IAM | Users list |
| 5 | RDS | DB instances + engine + status |
| 6 | Lambda | Functions + runtime + memory |
| 7 | EKS | Cluster names |
| 8 | ECS | Cluster ARNs |
| 9 | ECR | Repository names + URIs |
| 10 | ELB/ALB/NLB | Load balancer name + type + DNS |
| 11 | Auto Scaling | Group name + min/max/desired |
| 12 | CloudWatch | Alarms + state |
| 13 | Route53 | Hosted zones |
| 14 | SNS | Topic ARNs |
| 15 | SQS | Queue URLs |

---

## ⚙️ Prerequisites

```bash
# 1. AWS CLI must be installed
aws --version

# 2. AWS CLI must be configured
aws configure --profile default

# 3. Script must be executable
chmod +x aws_resource_list.sh
```

---

## 🚀 Usage

```bash
# Syntax
./aws_resource_list.sh <aws-region> <aws-profile>

# Example — us-east-1 with default profile
./aws_resource_list.sh us-east-1 default

# Example — Mumbai region with custom profile
./aws_resource_list.sh ap-south-1 myprofile
```

